    "scroll chiller"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Scroll chiller controller (BACnet option)",
  "applies_to": "Carrier AquaSnap 30MPA (condenserless) and 30MPW (water-cooled) 016-071 scroll chillers with ComfortLink controls and the factory BACnet communication option.",
  "summary": "This is the older ComfortLink generation of the 30MP, before the PIC6 Carrier Controller. BACnet MS/TP comes from a UPC Open controller in the main control box, which reads the ComfortLink chiller over CCN. The network points list has 126 objects: AVs, BVs and a few multistate values for start/stop, emergency stop, control point, setpoints, demand limit, water temperatures, refrigerant pressures, compressor status, run hours, strainer service and five user-defined points.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "Network number 16101 followed by the MAC address (MAC 20 gives 1610120)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Covers the ComfortLink 30MP (form 30MP-6T). Units with PIC6 controls (30MPW017-080, 30MPA/30MPQ021-080) use a different, larger object list.",
    "Object names end in _1; descriptions here are the printed point descriptions, with the CCN name added where two rows share a description (circuit A/B).",
    "Multistate values are printed as MSV (mapped as MV here). The Control Method states print '2 = Occupancy' and '3 = Occupancy' as shown; per the control text the methods are Switch, Occupancy and CCN.",
    "AV 8 Control Mode codes from the run status table: 0 Service Test, 1 Off Local, 2 Off CCN, 3 Off Time, 4 Off Emergency, 5 On Local, 6 On CCN, 7 On Time, 9 Pump Delay.",
    "AV 57 is printed as mr_mach_1 (CCN HR_MACH); kept as printed.",
    "AV 2901-2905 and BV 2911-2915 are user-defined points with no fixed meaning."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "AquaSnap 30MPA,MPW016-071 Liquid Chillers with Scroll Compressors and ComfortLink Controls - Controls, Start-Up, Operation, Service, and Troubleshooting (Appendix C, BACnet Communication Option, Table G Network Points List)",
    "doc_number": "30MP-6T",
    "revision_date": "10-23",
    "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1005/Public/0B/30MP-6T.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the UPC Open with its rotary switches, set the BAS port DIP switches for MS/TP and the baud rate, and set the chiller control method to CCN (Configuration > OPT2 > CTRL = 3). The BMS then starts and stops the chiller with BV 4 (CHIL_S_S), can write the control point and demand limit, and reads control mode, fluid temperatures, capacity and alarm state.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 4",
        "name": "chil_s_s_1",
        "why": "Network start/stop"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 6",
        "name": "emstop_1",
        "why": "Emergency stop command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 5",
        "name": "ctrl_pnt_1",
        "why": "Control point (leaving fluid setpoint)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "dem_lim_1",
        "why": "Demand limit, 0-100 %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 8",
        "name": "stat_1",
        "why": "Control mode code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 31",
        "name": "cool_lwt_1",
        "why": "Cooler leaving fluid temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 30",
        "name": "cool_ewt_1",
        "why": "Cooler entering fluid temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3",
        "name": "cap_t_1",
        "why": "Percent total capacity"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 59",
        "name": "alm_1",
        "why": "Alarm state (normal/alarm)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set the control method to CCN (Configuration > OPT2 > CTRL = 3) with the Enable/Off/Remote switch in Enable (or Remote with the contacts closed). The BMS then forces CHIL_S_S (BV 4) between Start and Stop; control mode reads 2 (Off CCN) or 6 (On CCN). Monitoring only does not need CTRL = 3.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The UPC Open speaks BACnet MS/TP at 9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k (Carrier default 76.8k), set on BAS port DIP switches DS1-DS2; 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
      "For MS/TP set DS3 to enable, DS4 to E1-485 and DS5-DS8 to MSTP; the EIA-485 jumpers must be set to EIA-485 and 2W.",
      "MAC address from the tens and ones rotary switches; switches and DIP settings are read only at power-up.",
      "Device instance defaults to network number 16101 followed by the MAC address (MAC 20 gives 1610120); change it with i-Vu Tools or a BACview.",
      "The UPC Open and the ComfortLink board must share the same CCN element and bus numbers (defaults 1 and 0).",
      "Fit a BT485 terminator on the first and last controller of the MS/TP segment."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "For the chiller to run, emstop_1 (BV 6) must be at Enable; writing EMSTOP stops all cooling at once.",
      "In Lead/Lag/Standby setups each chiller and UPC Open needs a unique CCN element number, with at most 3 UPC Opens per CCN bus.",
      "Pump, condenser and dual-setpoint points depend on unit options."
    ]
  },
